":0,"likeCount":2,"liked":false,"disliked":false},{"_id":"624152fd897253a6d15f7e51","commentBy":{"_id":"622b0cb171002d054a2de105","username":"Vynixu","verified":true,"role":"user","profilePicture":"/images/photo/622b0cb171002d054a2de105-1766397214454.png","createdAt":"2022-03-11T08:47:45.048Z","lastActive":"2026-10-07T18:28:26.593Z","status":"offline","id":"622b0cb171002d054a2de105","leaderboard":{"tag":null},"topMilestone":{"key":"creator.likes","tier":100}},"text":"First of all, you have to define the module itself, you do this as followed:\n\nlocal inviteModule = loadstring(game:HttpGet(\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/RegularVynixu/Utilities/main/Discord%20Inviter/Source.lua\"))()\n\nAfter you've defined the module, you may choose if you wish to make use of the invitation prompt, or just join the server.\nThe .Prompt function works as followed:\n\ninviteModule.Prompt({\nname = \"this is optional, it overwrites the server name displayed on the prompt\",\ninvite = \"your server invite here\",\n})\n\nNote that it will also prompt the invite on the user's Discord client, which is unpreventable.\n\nIf you wish to not make use of the invitation prompt, you would use the .Join function.\nThis function skips the prompt and directs the user to your server right away, however, it will still prompt on their Discord client.\n\ninviteModule.Join(\"your server invite here\")","createdAt":"2022-03-28T06:17:33.983Z","edited":true,"likeCount":1,"liked":false,"disliked":false},{"_id":"624ccae44d209d009547ba06","commentBy":{"_id":"61b91b8698ee0fd9d5778e8a","username":"Kaor","verified":true,"role":"user","profilePicture":"/images/photo/61b91b8698ee0fd9d5778e8a-1693028866881.png","createdAt":"2021-12-14T22:32:38.185Z","lastActive":"2024-11-06T19:33:30.738Z","status":"offline","id":"61b91b8698ee0fd9d5778e8a"},"text":"oShy is so  wierd ong","createdAt":"2022-04-05T23:04:04.534Z","edited":true,"dislikeCount":0,"likeCount":2,"liked":false,"disliked":false},{"_id":"624d05e8a75c74877d9